ing group and in order to  survive partners up with a lone wolf  abandoned by its pack it's a thrilling  gorgeously shot adventure but while the  film scored with critics it failed to  connect with audiences with an  advertising campaign which seemed to be  aimed more squarely at dog lovers than  fans of epic adventure alpha simply  didn't generate the kind of positive  word-of-mouth that it needed it also had  the misfortune of squaring off against  crazy rich Asians in the Meg two films  which destroyed at the box office  alpha failed to make back its budget  domestically but it seems destined for a  robust second life on home video  [Music]
 

